WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.848
Have you taken the red pill ?

00:00:01.848 --> 00:00:02.580
That means

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.098
not taking the blue pill

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.400
and waking up to the fact

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.140
that what you've been told

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.300
is often wrong.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.260
You take the blue pill.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.040
The phrase comes from the movie The Matrix.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.540
Believe whatever you want to believe.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.120
You take the red pill,

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.380
you stay in Wonderland

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.200
and I show you how deep the rabbit-hole goes.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.300
That moment in The Matrix,

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.980
Morpheus is offering him simply the truth.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.320
Candace Owens says she took the red pill

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.020
and now her YouTube channel

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.020
offers red pills

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.620
to millions of others.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:32.801
People don't care

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:33.880
to watch CNN

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:34.760
anymore.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.140
People are paying attention to YouTubers okay?

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.460
My second video

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.160
went trending worldwide with 80 million views.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.360
80 million?

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.320
80 million.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.090
It's obviously

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.080
the media's fault.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:45.940
In that video,

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.140
she mocked the media

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.530
for finding racism

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:49.380
everywhere.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.989
The persistence of racism in America.

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:53.735
The surge of hate,

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.140
the online racism.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.860
CNN was trying to sell to me,

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.260
as a black person,

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.640
that the KKK was alive and well.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:02.760
That was ridiculous.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.760
Oh my God, Charlottesville.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:07.240
White supremacy is alive and well.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.900
So I made a video just essentially making fun

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.200
of the narrative.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.580
How ridiculous that I should be

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:13.940
scared to go outside

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.400
because the KKK is alive and well.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.860
Another police shooting

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.200
of a black teen.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.640
She also complains that the media

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.640
imply

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.100
the biggest threat to young blacks

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.140
is the police.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:27.880
Police officer charged with murder caught on camera

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.620
shooting an unarmed black man.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.220
Fact number 1.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.280
Approximately 93 percent

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.240
of black homicide victims

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.160
are killed

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.320
by other black people.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.580
Police violence

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.620
is a real threat.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.200
No, it is not

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.260
and I will not allow you to say that either.

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:46.760
It is not a real threat, okay?

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.600
Some innocent people have been

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.960
tortured by police.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.210
That's absolutely right.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.170
Some innocent people

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.980
have also been struck by lightning.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.219
16 unarmed black men were

00:01:56.219 --> 00:01:58.720
killed by police officers in 2016.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.900
If you are watching CNN,

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:00.660
you would have thought

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.360
it was happening every single day,

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:03.720
okay that's a problem.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.040
16 represents point

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.040
zero zero zero zero four percent

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.540
of the black community.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:09.450
And yet there were riots,

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.582
and there were protests,

00:02:10.582 --> 00:02:11.740
and Black Lives Matter

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.820
has actually resulted in more black deaths

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.100
across the country

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.660
because police officers don't want to answer the call.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.830
It's not popular in the black community

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.400
to say such things

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:21.900
or

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.380
to say that you are conservative.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.320
Owens jokes in this video that

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.280
it's easier to tell your parents you're gay.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.380
Mom, Dad,

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.340
I'm a lesbian.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.520
I like girls.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.000
Oh sweetheart,

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.560
we always knew.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.100
Oh, thank you guys.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:44.860
Oh, also I think I might be a conservative.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.020
I don't understand.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.580
Guys it's totally fine.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:48.360
it's okay,

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.160
I just, you know

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.440
think a little more conservatively.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.780
But sweetheart,

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.100
you're black.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.560
Mom, I'm still black.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.100
I simply think that we should maybe

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.390
put the economical future of this

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.380
country ahead of the social issues,

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.780
that is all.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.440
Sweetie,

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.320
can you please just be gay?

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.980
It's more difficult to say to someone

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.500
I'm a conservative.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.800
Candace says the big issue facing blacks

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.600
is not racism or police shootings, it's

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.540
dependence on government

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.460
that began 50 years ago with

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.380
Lyndon Johnson's Great Society programs.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.120
They incentivized mothers, right,

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.520
to not to marry their fathers.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.120
That's why single motherhood is up.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.720
The government would give you more

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.040
if you didn't marry him.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.560
We are fully reliant on the government.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.500
My entire family is on welfare,

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.880
save a couple of people

00:03:34.882 --> 00:03:35.960
and what it does is

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.880
they essentially offer you some money

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.480
and then they say wherever you work, okay

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.240
you don't make enough

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.641
so we're gonna give you this much money

00:03:41.641 --> 00:03:42.180
on top of that.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.380
So they do what?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.560
They say, oh I don't want to make more

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.360
because the government is already giving me

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.480
five hundred that I don't want to lose and...

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.460
And your entire family's on welfare?

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.220
Yeah pretty much.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:52.620
My entire family's on welfare.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.640
And they still like you?

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:54.453
Yeah they love me.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.440
I'm great, right?

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.980
Oh celebrities,

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.540
now I rarely think about Russia.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.480
Fear absolutely dominates black people.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.100
Like hamsters on a wheel,

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.640
run, run, run, run, run, run.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.195
What the government has done successfully

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.360
is made people insecure.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:11.926
People don't think they can do anything

00:04:11.926 --> 00:04:12.810
without the government.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.960
We've got the government regulating nail salons,

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.220
eyebrow salons.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.120
The government has extended an overreach into

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.460
every single arena of our lives.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.360
The time is now

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.920
for black minds to be unleashed.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.740
People don't understand is how many black people are

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.340
so excited about what I'm doing,

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:29.060
how many black people see the opportunity,

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.700
and how many black people are very aware

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.360
that they have been duped by the left.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:33.840
She calls that

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.800
taking the red pill.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.460
Who else has taken the red pill?

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.580
Brandon Tatum,

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.210
he's got a pretty large following

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.560
Your success in life

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.080
is dependent upon you.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.840
There's CJ Pearson,

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.880
who says he's the left's youngest problem.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:48.860
Black lives,

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.016
they do matter.

00:04:50.016 --> 00:04:51.312
So do white lives, though.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:52.640
And I think why

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.100
some of these black conservatives

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.200
have not been successful in the past

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.560
is because they care too much

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.160
about what people thought.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.280
We're doing it differently.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.540
We are talking a lot of trash.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.860
We are very sassy.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:03.800
The African-American community is

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.340
suffering from a poor memory.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.420
We want people to know

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.400
you can feel free to call me an Uncle Tom,

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.420
you can feel free to call me an Auntie Tom

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:11.180
it does not affect me.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:12.060
Do you want to know why?

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.380
Because I actually read the book

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.760
